Overview
--------
Nexus Forge is an open-source, local-first Linux coding environment
where AI coding agents collaborate in real-time alongside one human.

It combines a 4-quadrant terminal cockpit with live animated avatar
sidebars, local LLM assistance via Ollama, shared semantic memory
(forge-db), and iterative context compaction.


What is Included in v1.0.0
--------------------------
1. 4 Terminal Quadrants (GTK3 + VTE 2.91)
   - Resizable 2x2 grid running independent tmux sessions.
   - Quadrant zoom: press Ctrl+Shift+Z or F11 (or double-click the header)
     to toggle full-window view.
   - Terminal reconnect overlay with crash-loop backoff protection.

2. Animated Avatar Sidebars
   - Real-time visual status for each agent (idle, working, final).
   - Helper avatar animations when Dushich assists in a quadrant.

3. Live Token Quota Badges
   - Real-time hourly and weekly rate limit usage meters for cloud agents.
   - Local indicator for offline inference.

4. Dushich: Local AI Collaborator
   - Local assistant running Qwen 27B on Ollama with 131k context.
   - Takes verified coding tasks through Model Context Protocol (MCP).
   - Executes in isolated Git workspaces with automated tests and checks.
   - Zero cloud token cost.

5. Forge Memory (forge-db)
   - SQLite shared memory for project tracking, atlas paths, and notes.
   - Semantic meaning search using vector embeddings (Ollama or FastEmbed).
   - Collision detection prevents conflicting agent work on shared projects.

6. Iterative Context Summarizer (dushich-summarizer)
   - Sentence-boundary window summarizer on local GPU.
   - Compacts massive logs, transcripts, and source files efficiently.

7. Turnkey Installer (./install.sh)
   - One-command setup for modern Linux (Ubuntu, Debian, Fedora, Arch).
   - Supports --check, --dry-run, and --config-only.
   - Automatically provisions local configurations with portable relative links.

8. User-Agnostic Launchers
   - Dynamically resolves user accounts and home directories.
   - Safe Git SSH guards that never overwrite environment variables.


Quickstart
----------
1. Clone the repository:
   git clone --branch v1.0.0 https://github.com/chu4urdolen/noobia.git
   cd noobia

2. Run the installer:
   ./install.sh

3. Start the cockpit:
   nexus-forge

Headless self-test (no display needed):
   python3 common/nexus_forge/nexus_forge.py --self-test


Customizing Quadrants
---------------------
Quadrants can be customized by editing ~/.config/nexus-forge/config.json
to point to any shell, local Ollama model, or tool.


Prerequisites
-------------
- Linux (Ubuntu 22.04+, Debian 12+, Fedora, Arch)
- Python 3.10+, GTK3, VTE 2.91, tmux
- Optional: Ollama (for local Qwen model), uv, chafa
